## Security findings to remediate
[
 {
  "id": "SEC-1",
  "severity": "high",
  "title": "Mutating and analytics endpoints have no authentication: anyone holding a short link can deactivate it or read its stats",
  "location": "app/api/links.py:27 (router has no auth dependency); app/api/links.py:103-113 (DELETE /api/links/{code}); app/api/links.py:116-137 (GET /api/links/{code}/stats); app/api/links.py:38 (POST /api/links)",
  "recommendation": "Short codes are shared publicly by design, so their unpredictability does not act as access control. Add a router-level dependency on the /api/links router, e.g. `APIRouter(prefix='/api/links', dependencies=[Depends(require_api_key)])`. It should compare the key from a secret setting in constant time using `hmac.compare_digest`. Better still, return a per-link management token at creation, store only its hash, and require it for DELETE and stats. Keep GET/HEAD /{code} public. Until this ships, restrict /api/links* at the gateway or by network policy (OPERATIONS.md already says so) and treat this as a release blocker for any public exposure."
 }
]

