   "description": "Pydantic v2 only; import nothing from other app packages. Use `import datetime as dt` so field names can be 'date'.\n\napp/schemas/links.py:\n- MAX_URL_LENGTH = 2048.\n- `def validate_target_url(value: str) -> str`: raise ValueError with a short message when any of these hold:\n  - len(value) == 0 or len(value) > 2048\n  - any char c with ord(c) <= 0x20, ord(c) == 0x7F, ord(c) > 0x7E, or c.isspace() (this rejects whitespace, control and non-ASCII characters)\n  - parsing fails: parts = urllib.parse.urlsplit(value) and parts.port are both evaluated inside try, and a ValueError there means 'invalid URL'\n  - parts.scheme.lower() not in {'http', 'https'}\n  - not value[len(parts.scheme):].startswith('://')\n  - not parts.netloc or not parts.hostname\n  Otherwise return value UNCHANGED (no normalization). Examples: 'HTTPS://example.com' is accepted. Rejected: 'javascript:alert(1)', 'data:text/html,hi', 'file:///etc/passwd', 'ftp://example.com', 'mailto:a@b.c', '/path', 'example.com', 'http://', 'https:///x', 'http://exa mple.com', and any URL containing \\n or \\t.\n- `class LinkCreate(BaseModel)`: url: StrictStr; a field_validator('url') calls validate_target_url. model_config = ConfigDict(json_schema_extra={'examples': [{'url': 'https://example.com/a?b=1'}]}).\n- `def _as_utc(v: dt.datetime | None) -> dt.datetime | None`: if naive, replace(tzinfo=dt.timezone.utc); otherwise astimezone(dt.timezone.utc).\n- `class LinkCreatedResponse(BaseModel)`: code: str; short_url: str; url: str; is_active: bool; created_at: dt.datetime, with a field_validator(mode='after') applying _as_utc.\n- `class LinkDetailResponse(LinkCreatedResponse)`: deactivated_at: dt.datetime | None = None (same UTC validator); total_clicks: int.\n- `class DailyClicks(BaseModel)`: date: dt.date; count: int.\n- `class ReferrerCount(BaseModel)`: referrer: str | None; count: int.\n- `class LinkStatsResponse(BaseModel)`: code: str; total_clicks: int; clicks_per_day: list[DailyClicks]; top_referrers: list[ReferrerCount].\n- `class ErrorResponse(BaseModel)`: detail: Any (used in OpenAPI `responses=`).\n\napp/schemas/health.py: `class HealthResponse(BaseModel)`: status: str.\n\napp/schemas/__init__.py re-exports all of the above.",
