   "title": "Services: codes, link lifecycle, redirect/clicks, stats",
   "description": "Never import fastapi or starlette. Import errors from app.core.errors, models from app.models, and repositories from app.repositories. Services commit and roll back themselves.\n\napp/services/codes.py:\n- ALPHABET = string.ascii_letters + string.digits\n- RESERVED_CODES = frozenset({'healthz', 'readyz', 'api', 'docs', 'redoc', 'openapi.json', 'static', 'favicon.ico'})\n- CODE_PATTERN = re.compile(r'^[A-Za-z0-9]{1,32}$')\n- `def generate_code(length: int) -> str`: ''.join(secrets.choice(ALPHABET) for _ in range(length)). Never use the random module.\n- `def is_reserved(code: str) -> bool`: code.casefold() in RESERVED_CODES.\n- `def is_valid_code_format(code: str) -> bool`: bool(CODE_PATTERN.fullmatch(code)).\n\napp/services/link_service.py (module logger = logging.getLogger('app.services.links')):\n- `@dataclass class CreateResult: link: Link; replayed: bool`\n- `@dataclass class LinkDetail: link: Link; total_clicks: int`\n- MAX_REFERRER_LEN = 2048, MAX_USER_AGENT_LEN = 512, MAX_IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_LEN = 255.\n- `def hash_ip(ip: str | None, salt: str | None) -> str | None`: if not ip or not salt, return None; otherwise hmac.new(salt.encode(), ip.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest().\n- `class LinkService.__init__(self, session: Session, *, code_length: int = 7, max_attempts: int = 5, ip_hash_salt: str | None = None)` builds LinkRepository, ClickRepository and IdempotencyRepository.\n\n`create_link(self, url: str, idempotency_key: str | None = None) -> CreateResult`:\n(a) If the key is not None and (key.strip() == '' or len(key) > 255), raise BadRequestError('Invalid Idempotency-Key header').\n(b) request_hash = hashlib.sha256(url.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest().\n(c) If a key is given: existing = idem_repo.get_by_key(key). If it exists, return self._replay_or_conflict(existing, request_hash).\n(d) Loop for attempt in range(max_attempts):\n  - code = codes.generate_code(self.code_length). Call it through the module (`from app.services import codes`) so tests can monkeypatch app.services.codes.generate_code.\n  - If codes.is_reserved(code): continue.\n  - link = Link(code=code, url=url, is_active=True); try link_repo.add(link); on IntegrityError call session.rollback() and continue.\n  - If a key is given: try idem_repo.add(IdempotencyKey(key=key, request_hash=request_hash, link_id=link.id)). On IntegrityError: session.rollback(); winner = idem_repo.get_by_key(key); if winner is None raise ConflictError('Idempotency-Key conflict, please retry'); otherwise return self._replay_or_conflict(winner, request_hash).\n  - session.commit(); return CreateResult(link=link, replayed=False). Attributes reload from the DB after commit.\n(e) After the loop: logger.error('short code allocation exhausted') and raise ServiceUnavailableError('Could not allocate a unique short code, please retry').\n\n`_replay_or_conflict(record, request_hash) -> CreateResult`: if record.request_hash != request_hash, raise ConflictError('Idempotency-Key already used with a different payload'). Otherwise load the link with session.get(Link, record.link_id) and return CreateResult(link, replayed=True).\n\n`_get_or_404(code) -> Link`: if not codes.is_valid_code_format(code), raise NotFoundError() without querying. Otherwise link = link_repo.get_by_code(code); raise NotFoundError() if it is None.\n\n`get_link_detail(code) -> LinkDetail`: returns the link (active or not) plus click_repo.count_for_link(link.id).\n\n`deactivate(code) -> None`: link = _get_or_404(code). If link.is_active: set is_active=False and deactivated_at=utcnow(), then commit. An already-inactive link is a no-op (deactivated_at unchanged).\n\n`resolve_for_redirect(code) -> str`: link = _get_or_404(code); if not link.is_active raise GoneError(); return link.url. This is used by HEAD and records no click.\n\n`resolve_and_record_click(code, referrer: str | None, user_agent: str | None, client_ip: str | None) -> str`: link = _get_or_404(code); if inactive raise GoneError(); url = link.url (read before any commit). Then try: click_repo.add(ClickEvent(link_id=link.id, referrer=referrer[:2048] if referrer else None, user_agent=user_agent[:512] if user_agent else None, ip_hash=hash_ip(client_ip, self.ip_hash_salt))); session.commit(). On `except Exception`: session.rollback() and logger.exception('failed to record click for link_id=%s', link.id), never logging the IP. Return url.\n\napp/services/stats_service.py:\n- `@dataclass class LinkStats: code: str; total_clicks: int; clicks_per_day: list[tuple[date, int]]; top_referrers: list[tuple[str | None, int]]`\n- TOP_REFERRERS_LIMIT = 10.\n- `class StatsService.__init__(self, session)` builds LinkRepository and ClickRepository.\n- `get_stats(self, code: str, days: int = 30, now: datetime | None = None) -> LinkStats`:\n  - If the code format is invalid or the link is missing, raise NotFoundError(). Deactivated links are allowed.\n  - now defaults to utcnow() (naive UTC; strip tzinfo after converting to UTC if one is passed).\n  - start_date = now.date() - timedelta(days=days - 1); since = datetime.combine(start_date, time.min).\n  - total = click_repo.count_for_link(link.id).\n  - per_day = Counter(ts.date() for ts in click_repo.created_at_since(link.id, since)), sorted ascending by date and returned as a list of (date, count).\n  - refs = click_repo.referrer_counts(link.id), sorted with key=lambda r: (-r[1], r[0] is None, r[0] or ''), sliced [:10].\n  - Return LinkStats.\n\napp/services/__init__.py stays empty.",
