   "description": "Create an empty app/api/__init__.py.\n\napp/api/deps.py:\n- `get_settings(request: Request) -> Settings`: return request.app.state.settings.\n- `get_link_service(db: Session = Depends(get_db), settings: Settings = Depends(get_settings)) -> LinkService`: LinkService(db, code_length=settings.short_code_length, max_attempts=settings.code_max_attempts, ip_hash_salt=settings.ip_hash_salt).\n- `get_stats_service(db: Session = Depends(get_db)) -> StatsService`.\n- `build_short_url(base_url: str, code: str) -> str`: base_url.rstrip('/') + '/' + code.\nget_db must be imported from app.core.db.\n\napp/api/links.py: router = APIRouter(prefix='/api/links', tags=['links']). Common error responses use ErrorResponse models.\n- `@router.post('', status_code=201, response_model=LinkCreatedResponse, responses={400,409,422,503})` `def create_link(payload: LinkCreate, response: Response, idempotency_key: str | None = Header(default=None, alias='Idempotency-Key'), service=Depends(get_link_service), settings=Depends(get_settings))`: result = service.create_link(payload.url, idempotency_key). Set response.headers['Location'] = f'/api/links/{code}'. If result.replayed, set response.headers['Idempotent-Replayed'] = 'true'. Return LinkCreatedResponse(code, short_url=build_short_url(...), url, is_active, created_at).\n- `@router.get('/{code}', response_model=LinkDetailResponse, responses={404})`: build from service.get_link_detail(code), adding deactivated_at and total_clicks.\n- `@router.delete('/{code}', status_code=204, response_class=Response, responses={404})`: service.deactivate(code); return Response(status_code=204).\n- `@router.get('/{code}/stats', response_model=LinkStatsResponse, responses={404,422})` `def get_stats(code: str, days: int = Query(30, ge=1, le=365), service=Depends(get_stats_service))`: map LinkStats to the response (DailyClicks(date=d, count=c), ReferrerCount(referrer=r, count=c)).\n\napp/api/redirect.py: router = APIRouter(tags=['redirect']).\n- `@router.get('/{code}', status_code=307, response_class=Response, responses={307: {'description': 'Redirect to original URL'}, 404: ..., 410: ...})` `def redirect(code: str, request: Request, service=Depends(get_link_service))`: url = service.resolve_and_record_click(code, request.headers.get('referer'), request.headers.get('user-agent'), request.client.host if request.client else None). Return Response(status_code=307, headers={'Location': url, 'Cache-Control': 'no-store'}). Do NOT use RedirectResponse, which quotes the URL.\n- `@router.head('/{code}', include_in_schema=False)`: same response, built with service.resolve_for_redirect(code); records no click.\n\napp/api/health.py: router = APIRouter(tags=['health']).\n- `@router.get('/healthz', response_model=HealthResponse)` returns {'status': 'ok'} with no DB dependency.\n- `@router.get('/readyz', response_model=HealthResponse, responses={503})` `def readyz(db: Session = Depends(get_db))`: try db.execute(text('SELECT 1')); except Exception: logging.getLogger('app.health').warning('readiness check failed') and raise ServiceUnavailableError('Database is not ready'). Return {'status': 'ready'}.\n\napp/main.py: `def create_app(settings: Settings | None = None) -> FastAPI`:\n- settings = settings or Settings(); configure_logging(settings.log_level).\n- engine = create_db_engine(settings.database_url); session_factory = create_session_factory(engine).\n- @asynccontextmanager lifespan(app): Base.metadata.create_all(bind=engine); yield; engine.dispose().\n- app = FastAPI(title='URL Shortener', version='1.0.0', lifespan=lifespan); set app.state.settings, app.state.engine and app.state.session_factory.\n- register_exception_handlers(app); app.add_middleware(RequestLoggingMiddleware).\n- Include routers in EXACTLY this order: health.router, links.router, redirect.router (the catch-all goes last).\n- Return app. At module level: `app = create_app()`.\n- Import Base from app.models so that all tables register.\n- Docstring note: