 "test_strategy": "pytest with fastapi.testclient.TestClient, owned by the test agent.\n\nIsolation: a fixture builds `settings = Settings(database_url=f\"sqlite:///{tmp_path}/test.db\", base_url=\"http://sho.rt\")`, then `app = create_app(settings)`, and yields `with TestClient(app) as client:`. The context manager is mandatory so that the lifespan create_all runs. Every test docstring starts with 'Covers: FR-n[, NFR-m]'.\n\nKey techniques:\n(1) Redirects: client.get(f'/{code}', follow_redirects=False); assert 307, the exact Location, and Cache-Control no-store.\n(2) Forced collision: monkeypatch.setattr('app.services.codes.generate_code', fake). The fake returns an existing code first and then a fresh one, always the same code (expect 503 with no traceback), or 'healthz' first (reserved, then fresh).\n(3) Uniqueness: insert a duplicate Link through a session from app.state.session_factory and expect sqlalchemy.exc.IntegrityError. Create 1000 links via the API and check that all codes are unique and match ^[A-Za-z0-9]{7}$.\n(4) Idempotency: same key and same body give identical bodies with exactly one Idempotent-Replayed header and one row; a different url gives 409; an empty or 256-char key gives 400; the race is simulated per RK-6.\n(5) Click privacy: send requests with X-Forwarded-For: 203.0.113.7, scan every column of every click_events row plus caplog text for '203.0.113.7' and 'testclient', and check ip_hash is null without a salt or equals hmac.new(salt, b'testclient', sha256).hexdigest() with Settings(ip_hash_salt='s').\n(6) Stats day bucketing: insert ClickEvent rows directly with created_at set to 23:59:59 yesterday and 00:00:01 today (UTC, naive), relative to datetime.now(timezone.utc). Also check the days=0/366 422 cases, top-referrer ordering and the limit of 10.\n(7) Readiness failure: app.dependency_overrides[app.core.db.get_db] = a generator yielding a stub whose execute() raises sqlalchemy.exc.OperationalError('SELECT 1', {}, Exception('boom')); expect 503 and a body without 'boom'.\n(8) 500 handling: either app.add_api_route('/_test/boom', raising_endpoint) (a multi-segment path, so the catch-all cannot match it) or monkeypatch LinkService.get_link_detail to raise RuntimeError('secret'). Assert the body is exactly {'detail': 'Internal Server Error'} and that caplog has the traceback. Use TestClient(app, raise_server_exceptions=False) as a safety net.\n(9) Click failure: monkeypatch ClickRepository.add to raise SQLAlchemyError; expect 307 still returned and a warning/error logged.\n(10) Request log: caplog record from logger 'app.request' has attributes method, path, status and duration_ms.\n(11) OpenAPI: check the paths and the named schemas LinkCreatedResponse, LinkDetailResponse and LinkStatsResponse.\n(12) Optional performance test (NFR-4), marked slow: 10k links seeded, 500 redirects and 200 creations, p95 checked.\n\nTarget: at least 85% line coverage of app/ (pytest --cov=app).",
 "config": [
  "DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./shortener.db (SQLAlchemy URL; for SQLite, check_same_thread=False is applied automatically)",
  "BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000 (trailing slash stripped when building short_url)",
  "SHORT_CODE_LENGTH=7 (int, 4..32)",
  "CODE_MAX_ATTEMPTS=5 (int, 1..20; collision retries before 503)",
  "IP_HASH_SALT= (optional; empty or unset means ip_hash is stored as NULL)",
  "LOG_LEVEL=INFO (DEBUG|INFO|WARNING|ERROR)"
 ]
